  "answer_text": "Cato Sockets do not support jumbo frames on LAN ports. For a 9000-byte frame received on a LAN port, the Socket checks the DF (Don’t Fragment) bit: if DF is not set, the packet is accepted and fragmented to conform to the 1500-byte MTU; if DF is set, the packet is dropped and an ICMP Fragmentation Needed message is returned to the sender.",
